/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A truss fuselage is a frame of metal tubes with diagonal wires and fabric covering.
   - A monocoque shell is different.
   - A semi-monocoque shell puts a skeleton back under a thin skin.
   - In a semi-monocoque fuselage the skin is a thin sheet of aluminium alloy or composite.
   - Pressure is the clearest load.
   - σh is hoop stress in Pa; p is differential pressure in Pa; r is radius in m; t is skin thickness in m.
   - σl is longitudinal stress in Pa; the symbols are the same.
   - The hoop stress is twice the longitudinal stress.
*/
